s in this range indicate the highest priority. The analysis requires a verification to detect if the most recent updates are present, or have reverted.\n\n\n**Identifying data integrity issues**\n\nInitial assessment highlights several data integrity issues: loss of cell formatting (3,026 cells reverted to default), address/zip code omissions (81 and 15 instances respectively), and missing NICE industry codes (27 cases). Row 12,288 shows the most recent update of the corporate registration number. Data from rows 702 to 5,500 includes 5 instances of incorrectly recorded corporate numbers for individual businesses.\n\n\n**Validating business registration numbers**\n\nThe current focus is to validate business registration numbers. First, removing the corporate registration number from individual businesses as these are not registered corporations. Further assessment involves checking the modulo 11 check digit for consistency, identifying 11 discrepancies. Finally, address and postal code omissions must be identified and addressed.\n\nThe second data segment (rows 11,847-12,346) is now being evaluated. Here, 2 instances of incorrect corporate registration numbers for individual businesses have been identified. The dataset has normal (401), closed (96), and temporary (3) operational statuses.\n\n\n"}
